{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X61MQCZNhCbEcQskKUAw3f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources/\"\n3\tsource_raw: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources.md\"\n4\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T09:52:00-0400\"\n5\tauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs), CC BY 4.0\"\n6\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.3\"]\n7\tconcepts_covered: [\"node-allocatable\", \"node-capacity\", \"requests-as-scheduling-input\", \"podfitsresources\"]\n8\tcloses_gap: \"ch-07 outline Open Question #8 — 'available resources' in the PodFitsResources description is measured against allocatable, not capacity. Previously the relationship between the two words was named but not defined in any cached source.\"\n9\tscope_note: \"Deliberately shallow. The reservation model itself (kube-reserved, system-reserved, eviction thresholds, cgroup enforcement) is Chapter 8's territory and was not extracted.\"\n10\t---\n11\t# Node Allocatable (kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources/)\n12\t\n13\t> **Extraction note.** All passages below are **[VERBATIM]** and safe to cite.\n14\t\n15\t## What Allocatable is\n16\t\n17\t> 'Allocatable' on a Kubernetes node is defined as the amount of compute resources that\n18\t> are available for pods.\n19\t\n20\t## What the scheduler does with it\n21\t\n22\t> The scheduler treats 'Allocatable' as the available `capacity` for pods.\n23\t\n24\t> The scheduler does not over-subscribe 'Allocatable'.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\tNOT IN THIS SNAPSHOT: the formula or diagram relating node Capacity to `kube-reserved`,\n29\t`system-reserved`, `eviction-threshold` and Allocatable. The source presents this as an\n30\timage (`node-capacity.svg`) with no text equivalent, so no equation is extractable. **§2\n31\tmust not state an arithmetic relationship between capacity and allocatable.** The two\n32\tsentences above are sufficient for what §2 needs — that allocatable is the number the\n33\treader should be doing arithmetic against. See research-manifest Gaps, G-7C.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5775eff9-d29f-49ec-9e8e-059f81638978","uuid":"b08f881a-e899-4ac4-8ef0-a5df9164edad","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:36:56.570Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\k8s-docs-node-allocatable-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources/\"\nsource_raw: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T09:52:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs), CC BY 4.0\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.3\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"node-allocatable\", \"node-capacity\", \"requests-as-scheduling-input\", \"podfitsresources\"]\ncloses_gap: \"ch-07 outline Open Question #8 — 'available resources' in the PodFitsResources description is measured against allocatable, not capacity. Previously the relationship between the two words was named but not defined in any cached source.\"\nscope_note: \"Deliberately shallow. The reservation model itself (kube-reserved, system-reserved, eviction thresholds, cgroup enforcement) is Chapter 8's territory and was not extracted.\"\n---\n# Node Allocatable (kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources/)\n\n> **Extraction note.** All passages below are **[VERBATIM]** and safe to cite.\n\n## What Allocatable is\n\n> 'Allocatable' on a Kubernetes node is defined as the amount of compute resources that\n> are available for pods.\n\n## What the scheduler does with it\n\n> The scheduler treats 'Allocatable' as the available `capacity` for pods.\n\n> The scheduler does not over-subscribe 'Allocatable'.\n\n---\n\nNOT IN THIS SNAPSHOT: the formula or diagram relating node Capacity to `kube-reserved`,\n`system-reserved`, `eviction-threshold` and Allocatable. The source presents this as an\nimage (`node-capacity.svg`) with no text equivalent, so no equation is extractable. **§2\nmust not state an arithmetic relationship between capacity and allocatable.** The two\nsentences above are sufficient for what §2 needs — that allocatable is the number the\nreader should be doing arithmetic against. See research-manifest Gaps, G-7C.\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}}}
