{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011yrKexzvVj6RGuf9U1gfU4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/configure-upgrade-etcd/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T03:14:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.1\", \"D1 Administration\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"etcd\", \"etcd-access\", \"api-server-as-front-end\", \"control-plane\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Operating etcd clusters for Kubernetes - definition and access control (kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/configure-upgrade-etcd/)\n9\t\n10\t> **Snapshot note.** This snapshot COMPLEMENTS and does not supersede\n11\t> `k8s-docs-etcd-backup-2026-08-23.md`, which covers the backup/restore portion of the SAME page.\n12\t> Two snapshots share this source_url by design: the 08-23 file carries the Chapter 8\n13\t> backup material, this 08-24 file carries the two sentences Chapter 3 sec.2/sec.5 depend on.\n14\t> Only sentences verified character-for-character against the rendered page are transcribed here.\n15\t> The page's TLS configuration guidance (peer/client certs, --client-cert-auth, --trusted-ca-file)\n16\t> was NOT transcribed - it is Chapter 8 material and was not verbatim-verified in this pass.\n17\t\n18\tOpening definition:\n19\t\n20\t\"etcd is a consistent and highly-available key value store used as Kubernetes' backing store for all cluster data.\"\n21\t\n22\tFrom the securing/access-control guidance:\n23\t\n24\t\"Access to etcd is equivalent to root permission in the cluster so ideally only the API server should have access to it.\"\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5775eff9-d29f-49ec-9e8e-059f81638978","uuid":"ff97d178-6214-437d-8001-a4fdffc3fe9d","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:36:57.288Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\k8s-docs-etcd-access-control-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/configure-upgrade-etcd/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T03:14:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.1\", \"D1 Administration\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"etcd\", \"etcd-access\", \"api-server-as-front-end\", \"control-plane\"]\n---\n# Operating etcd clusters for Kubernetes - definition and access control (kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/configure-upgrade-etcd/)\n\n> **Snapshot note.** This snapshot COMPLEMENTS and does not supersede\n> `k8s-docs-etcd-backup-2026-08-23.md`, which covers the backup/restore portion of the SAME page.\n> Two snapshots share this source_url by design: the 08-23 file carries the Chapter 8\n> backup material, this 08-24 file carries the two sentences Chapter 3 sec.2/sec.5 depend on.\n> Only sentences verified character-for-character against the rendered page are transcribed here.\n> The page's TLS configuration guidance (peer/client certs, --client-cert-auth, --trusted-ca-file)\n> was NOT transcribed - it is Chapter 8 material and was not verbatim-verified in this pass.\n\nOpening definition:\n\n\"etcd is a consistent and highly-available key value store used as Kubernetes' backing store for all cluster data.\"\n\nFrom the securing/access-control guidance:\n\n\"Access to etcd is equivalent to root permission in the cluster so ideally only the API server should have access to it.\"\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
